From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:35:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] h713: v2: take the panel supply from the kernel tree

Kernel 0221 describes the V2 panel's supply (vcc-panel on PH19) and
reset (PH16) in the tree U-Boot shares, so drop the private copy 0015
added here. Both were named /regulator-panel and would merge, taking the
kernel's regulator-boot-on, which U-Boot reads as "switch on at init"
ahead of h713_disp_panel_initial_off(). Delete it for U-Boot, as the
bench board's -u-boot.dtsi does. The pins and the off delay are unchanged,
so U-Boot drives the panel exactly as before.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -1,17 +1,8 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
 
-#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include "sun50i-h713-u-boot.dtsi"
 
 / {
-	reg_panel_v2: regulator-panel {
-		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
-		regulator-name = "vcc-panel";
-		gpio = <&pio 7 19 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;	/* PH19 */
-		enable-active-high;
-		off-on-delay-us = <250000>;
-	};
-
 	/*
 	 * Standard Boot: boot only from the eMMC (mmc1) and only through the
 	 * RAUC A/B method. Declaring a bootmeth here binds just that one,
@@ -27,7 +18,14 @@
 	};
 };
 
-&display {
-	power-supply = <&reg_panel_v2>;
-	panel-reset-gpios = <&pio 7 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PH16 */
+/*
+ * The panel's supply (PH19) and reset (PH16) now come from the kernel tree
+ * (0221), as the bench board's do. In U-Boot, regulator-boot-on means
+ * "switch on at init"; the panel must come up inside the display sequence,
+ * after h713_disp_panel_initial_off(), so U-Boot leaves the supply off until
+ * h713_disp enables it. Linux keeps the property: there it means the
+ * bootloader left the supply on.
+ */
+&reg_panel {
+	/delete-property/ regulator-boot-on;
 };
